{%- comment -%}
  Renders <option> tags for the Bank Payment Checkout shipping-address form's
  country field (Slice 2C task 2C-6, docs/specs/SLICE-2C-BANK-PAYMENT-CHECKOUT.md
  criterion 94, D20).

  DELIBERATELY NOT Shopify's classic `{{ country_option_tags }}` object: that
  tag's <option> VALUES are country NAMES ("United States"), not ISO 3166-1
  alpha-2 codes, because it targets the classic customer address form's
  `address[country]` field. `/apps/carat/bank-checkout`'s `shippingAddress
  .countryCode` schema requires a 2-letter code (see
  apps.carat.bank-checkout.tsx's `shippingAddressRequestSchema`), so a
  name-valued <option> would silently fail server-side validation.

  A CURATED LIST, NOT EXHAUSTIVE. CaratForUs is a US-dollar, US-first MVP1
  jewelry business (README.md) — this list favors the US, Canada and common
  international shipping destinations rather than every ISO territory.
  Extend it if a real order needs a country not listed; the server does not
  validate countryCode against a fixed list ("Shopify is the authority on
  postal validity" — see the route's schema comment), so adding an <option>
  here is the only change needed.

  Accepts:
  - selected_country_code: {String} the ISO code to pre-select (optional).
    Defaults to "US" when blank, matching the schema's expectation that most
    orders ship domestically and keeping the field usably pre-filled for a
    guest who never had a stored address (D20 — a customer account is never
    required).

  Usage:
  {% render 'bank-checkout-country-options', selected_country_code: customer.default_address.country_code %}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign selected = selected_country_code | default: 'US'
-%}
<option value="US"{% if selected == 'US' %} selected{% endif %}>United States</option>
<option value="CA"{% if selected == 'CA' %} selected{% endif %}>Canada</option>
